# SitePro Dashboard

When working inside `apps/dashboard`:

- Read and follow `apps/dashboard/AGENTS.md`.
- Treat Laravel as the authoritative backend/domain layer.
- Keep routes thin and organize application behavior by feature.
- Do not scatter API requests through UI components.
- Do not duplicate backend authorization or business rules in Next.js.
- Do not introduce global state, new dependencies, or abstraction layers
  without a demonstrated need.
- Keep feature-specific code inside the feature that owns it.
- Consult relevant `/docs` files when product behavior is involved.